    <statement><p>Write out all functions <m>f: \{1,2,3,4\} \to \{a,b\}</m> (using two-line notation).</p>
<p>How many functions are there?</p>
<p><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>How many are surjective?</p>
<p><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>How many are injective?</p>
<p><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>How many are bijective?</p>
<p><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>16</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>14</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>There are 16 different functions. 
None of the functions are injective. Exactly 14 of the functions are surjective (there are 2 that are not: those that send everything to <m>a</m> or everything to <m>b</m>). No functions are both (since no functions here are injective).</p>
</solution>
